# Transient lint fixtures. The boundary, wiring, anti-slop and shadcn suites
# name their fixtures with these markers. Since genie-ops-center-v2-fa5m they
# write each fixture into a throwaway root that overlays the checkout, so they
# no longer write into the checkout. The one writer left is
# packages/config/src/oxlint/fixture-visibility.test.ts: it writes marked probes
# into a real project path to prove this file, while other projects' lint
# targets scan the same tree. A scan that lists a probe and opens it after the
# suite removed it fails with a bare ENOENT (genie-ops-center-v2-64a is the
# typecheck face of the same race; the root tsconfig excludes these markers for
# it). The entries also cover a future suite that writes into the checkout.
#
# Each pattern matches its marker anywhere inside a path segment, not only at
# the start, because a suite may name a fixture mid-basename: the config probes
# are `vitest.__boundary__.config.ts`, whose marker follows the dot. A `**/*`
# prefix covers the leading and the mid-basename shape alike, so one entry per
# marker is enough (genie-ops-center-v2-5hq).
#
# The harness lints an explicit fixture path with --no-ignore, so the fixtures
# themselves are still checked by the rules they exist to prove.
**/*__boundary__*
**/*__wiring__*
**/*__antislop__*
**/*__shadcn__*
